    "scope": "14.e.W adds apply_import_plan for explicit already-parsed artifact candidates. Fresh and saved plans undergo the same mapping/conflict/loss/complete-target assessment before the shared native writer performs live checks, locking, authorization, journaling, publication, receipt and cleanup. A saved envelope never supplies authority. Native exceptions and recovery states propagate without automatic retry or rollback. submitted_import_plan is passive and belongs to this call; execution separately reports actual native publication or historical replay. Replays retain original actor/time/plan/created IDs/receipt and do not claim a newly verified current target. No-ops require authorization but create no receipt or revision. Existing attachment bytes remain bound and unchanged. CLI/source parsing, incoming attachment creation, relation/registry imports, loss-acceptance workflow and the full import-specific crash/recovery matrix remain open; this is not full requirement or release completion."
